  "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e85-5t,3+2t,-4+7t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e85-5t,3+2t,-4+7t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e82,3,1\u27e9 & =30 \\\\ \u27e85-5t,3+2t,-4+7t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,3,1\u27e9 & =30 \\\\ 2(5-5t)+3(3+2t)-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 10-10t+9+6t-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 3t & =15 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e85-5(5),3+2(5),-4+7(5)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-20,13,31\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-20,13,31).$",
